The '''2022 EFL Cup final''' was the final of the [[2021–22 EFL Cup]]. It was played between [[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]] and [[Liverpool F.C.|Liverpool]] at [[Wembley Stadium]] in London, England, on 27 February 2022. The match saw no goals in the initial 90 minutes or the additional 30 minutes of extra time and went to a [[Penalty shoot-out (association football)|penalty shoot-out]]; each of the first 21 kicks in the shoot-out was scored before Chelsea goalkeeper [[Kepa Arrizabalaga]] missed his to give Liverpool an 11–10 victory and a record ninth EFL Cup title.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/60450274 |title=Chelsea 0–0 Liverpool |first=Phil|last=McNulty |website=BBC Sport |date=27 February 2022 |access-date=27 February 2022}}</ref>

It was the first EFL Cup final since [[2017 EFL Cup final|2017]] not to feature [[Manchester City F.C.|Manchester City]], who had been knocked out in the fourth round by [[West Ham United F.C.|West Ham United]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Holders Manchester City knocked out of the Carabao Cup |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/58976565 |website=BBC Sport |date=27 October 2021 |access-date=27 October 2021 }}</ref>

